! Proposed Definitions And Examples

!! cmavo: da'e (KOhA2)

!!! Proposed Definition
A pro-sumti for an utterance that will appear in the text much later than the current utterance.

!!! See Also
* {da'u}
* {de'e}
* {di'e}
* {la'e}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* much later utterance

!!! Usage Examples
;mi ba cusku .i la'e da'e jenca: "I will tell you. It (what will be told) is shocking."
;da'e poi se cusku mi cu melbi: "What I'm going to say (in the future) is beautiful."

!!! Notes
The utterance that this cmavo refers to is text. Using this cmavo alone refers to the words and rhetoric of the utterance. In constrast, prefixing this cmavo with {la'e} refers to what the text ''means''.

The "much later" part of the definition is defined to be in contrast with {de'e}, which refers to a utterance coming soon in the future. In other words, this cmavo refers to an utterance that will appear later than the utterance referred to by {de'e}.

!!! Issues
None.

!! cmavo: da'u (KOhA2)

!!! Proposed Definition
A pro-sumti for an utterance that appeared in the text much earlier than the current utterance.

!!! See Also
* {da'e}
* {de'e}
* {di'e}
* {la'e}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* much earlier utterance

!!! Usage Examples
;do pu cusku .ije la'e da'u jenca: "I told you, and it (what was told) was shocking."
;da'u poi se cusku mi cu melbi: "What I said (in the past) is beautiful."

!!! Notes
The utterance that this cmavo refers to is text. Using this cmavo alone refers to the words and rhetoric of the utterance. In constrast, prefixing this cmavo with {la'e} refers to what the text ''means''.

The "much earlier" part of the definition is defined to be in contrast with {de'u}, which refers to a recent utterance said in the near past. In other words, this cmavo refers to an utterance that appeared earlier than the utterance referred to by {de'e}.

!!! Issues
None.

!! cmavo: de'e (KOhA2)

!!! Proposed Definition
A pro-sumti for an utterance that will appear in the text very soon, after the current utterance.

!!! See Also
* {da'u}
* {de'e}
* {di'e}
* {la'e}

!!! Proposed Keywords
* later utterance

!!! Usage Examples
;la'e de'e jenca: "It (what is about to be said) is shocking."
;de'e poi se cusku mi cu melbi: "It (what I'm about to say) is beautiful."

!!! Notes
The utterance that this cmavo refers to is text. Using this cmavo alone refers to the words and rhetoric of the utterance. In constrast, prefixing this cmavo with {la'e} refers to what the text ''means''.

The "very soon" part of the definition is defined to be in contrast with {da'e}, which refers to a utterance coming very far in the future. In other words, this cmavo refers to an utterance that will appear in the future but still earlier than the utterance referred to by {da'e}.

!!! Issues
None.

!! Proposed Definition of ''de'u''

;__de'u__ (KOhA2): recent utterance -- pro-sumti: a recent utterance --
